---
// « Mentions légales » (LCEN art. 6-III) — the ENGLISH twin, written by a human rather than
// translated. TEXT page: pure Astro, no island, zero JS — the only one on the site in that case,
// and the only one exercising ADR-0002's SSG rationale. Do not add interactivity here without
// reason: its value is being readable without running a line of script.
//
// The shell lives in `layouts/Page.astro` — which adds no script, so the zero-JS promise holds.
// The page’s own text stylesheet goes through the `page-style` slot; the LEGAL TEXT itself stays
// here rather than in `copy.*` (yuya's decision): it is a REFERENCE text, read as a block and not
// by table entries, and its English version is a TWIN page written by a human.
import { DEFAULT_LOCALE, type Locale, localePath } from '../../i18n/locales';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { headCopy } from '../../ui/head-copy';

const locale = (Astro.currentLocale ?? DEFAULT_LOCALE) as Locale;
const head = headCopy(locale);
---

<Page title={head.legalTitle} description={head.legalDescription} path="/mentions-legales">
  <style is:global slot="page-style">
    main {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 20px 80px;
    }
    .back {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 11px;
      color: #8b98c0; /* NAVY.textMuted */
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
    .back:hover {
      color: #2fd4f0;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 22px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin: 0 0 32px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.4;
      color: #dde4f4; /* NAVY.textHeading */
      margin: 36px 0 12px;
    }
    p,
    li {
      font-size: 12px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: #aab6d6; /* NAVY.textBody */
    }
    p {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    ul {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      padding-left: 18px;
    }
    li {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    strong {
      color: #c8d2e8; /* NAVY.textSecondary */
    }
    .dim {
      font-size: 11px;
      color: #66739a; /* NAVY.textDim */
      margin-top: 36px;
    }
  </style>
    <main>
      <a class="back" href={localePath(locale, '/')}>← Back</a>

      <h1>Legal notice</h1>

      <h2>Publisher</h2>
      <p>
        PanoptiCool is published on a non-professional, non-profit basis by <strong>Yuya</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Contact: <a href="mailto:yuya@panopti.cool">yuya@panopti.cool</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Host</h2>
      <p>
        OVH SAS — 2 rue Kellermann, 59100 Roubaix, France<br />
        Phone: 1007 · RCS Lille Métropole 424 761 419<br />
        <a href="https://www.ovhcloud.com/fr/">ovhcloud.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Personal data</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>PanoptiCool collects nothing.</strong> This isn't a promise, it's a consequence of
        how it's built.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your export never leaves your device.</strong> It is not sent, uploaded or stored:
          the site is a set of static files, and the analysis runs in your browser. There is no
          server to send it to.
        </li>
        <li><strong>No cookies</strong>, no trackers, no analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>No account</strong>, no forms, no sign-up.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No connection logs.</strong> The server that serves you this page keeps neither
          your IP address nor your visit.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        There is therefore no processing of personal data within the meaning of the GDPR. There is
        no right of access, rectification or erasure to exercise: there is nothing to consult,
        correct or delete.
      </p>

      <h2>The AI analysis, if you use it</h2>
      <p>
        The results page offers to have your comments and searches read by a language model. That
        model runs <strong>on your own machine</strong>, in a server you start yourself. Nothing is
        sent to a third party, and this analysis only begins when you explicitly click.
      </p>

      <h2>What PanoptiCool displays</h2>
      <p>
        The tool shows what an algorithm <em>could</em> infer from a data export. It is not a
        diagnosis, nor a verdict on a person: it is a demonstration of a system. The inferences
        shown can be wrong, and when they are, that is also the point.
      </p>

      <h2>Code and licence</h2>
      <p>
        The code is free software, under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html"
          >AGPL-3.0-only</a
        > licence. You can read it, check it and reuse it:
        <a href="https://github.com/lagayayuya/PanoptiCool">github.com/lagayayuya/PanoptiCool</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="dim">
        This page is an English translation provided for convenience. The French version (<a
          href={localePath('fr', '/mentions-legales')}>mentions légales</a
        >) is the legally binding text.
      </p>
    </main>
</Page>
